---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
---
<Site title="What we believe — British Reformed Fellowship">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12">
    <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-oxblood">What we believe</p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl tracking-tight mt-3 text-balance">Holding fast the faithful Word.</h1>
    <p class="font-serif text-lg text-muted mt-5 max-w-2xl">The doctrines summarised below are those of the historic Reformed churches of the British Isles — set out in the Westminster Confession of Faith and the Larger and Shorter Catechisms.</p>

    <div class="prose-section">
      <h2>The Bible</h2>
      <p>The books of the Old and New Testaments are the inspired and infallible Word of God. They are the only sure rule of faith and obedience.</p>

      <h2>God</h2>
      <p>There is one true and living God, infinite in being and perfection, eternal, immutable, almighty, and most holy. He exists in three persons — Father, Son, and Holy Spirit — of one substance, equal in power and glory.</p>

      <h2>Creation and Providence</h2>
      <p>God created the heavens and the earth, and upholds and governs all things by His sovereign providence, working all things after the counsel of His own will.</p>

      <h2>Sin and the Fall</h2>
      <p>Our first parents, being tempted by Satan, sinned against God. By that sin they fell from their original righteousness, and we, their descendants, are by nature children of wrath, inclined to evil, and unable of ourselves to do what is pleasing to God.</p>

      <h2>Christ the Mediator</h2>
      <p>The Son of God, the second person of the Trinity, took to Himself the nature of man and became true God and true man in two distinct natures and one person. He fulfilled all righteousness for His people, and bore the full penalty of their sin upon the cross. He rose again the third day, ascended into heaven, and ever lives to make intercession.</p>

      <h2>Salvation by Grace</h2>
      <p>Salvation is the free gift of God's grace, through the work of Christ, received by faith alone. The grace of God is the efficient cause of faith; those whom God has chosen in Christ from before the foundation of the world are, in time, effectually called, justified, sanctified, and at last glorified.</p>

      <h2>The Church</h2>
      <p>The visible church is the whole number of God's people gathered under Christ the head. It is marked by the preaching of the Word, the administration of the sacraments of baptism and the Lord's Supper, and the exercise of discipline.</p>

      <h2>The Last Things</h2>
      <p>Christ will come again to judge the living and the dead. The dead shall be raised, and every person shall give account at the last judgement. The wicked shall depart into everlasting punishment, and the righteous into everlasting life.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 border-t border-rule pt-8 font-sans text-sm">
      <a href="/s/BRF-Confession.pdf" class="text-oxblood no-underline hover:underline">Read the full Westminster Confession of Faith (PDF) →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Site>

<style is:global>
  .prose-section { font-family: var(--font-serif); margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  .prose-section p { font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-ink); margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .prose-section h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: var(--color-oxblood); }
  .prose-section ul { list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .prose-section li { font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-top: 0.5rem; }
</style>
